# The owner's request after step 15 (2026-11-16): the core instructions
# tell the agent to stay inside its project, and to ask the user for what
# the workspace and the conversation do not hold.
#
# A break is matched by token, and the constant is one string literal, so
# the line is dropped where section 1 is put into the prompt: the bullet is
# one line of the string (its source lines end in `\`).

[break] the-prompt-without-the-stay-in-project-line
rule: Section 1 of the system prompt tells the agent to stay inside its project and ask the user, not to look in other projects' files.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/context/prompt.rs
in: build
find: vec![CORE_INSTRUCTIONS.to_owned()]
replace: vec![CORE_INSTRUCTIONS.lines().filter(|line| !line.starts_with("- Stay inside")).collect::<Vec<_>>().join("\n")]
caught-by:
    cineris-agent context::prompt::tests::the_core_instructions_keep_the_agent_inside_its_project
    cineris-agent context::prompt::tests::the_guided_style_adds_its_notes_after_the_environment
